.TH SLIVERBAR 1 "July 2026" "sliverbar @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliverbar \- lightweight native X11 panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliverbar
.RI [ \-\-config\ PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-check-config ]
.RB [ \-\-diagnose ]
.RB [ \-\-list-pim-sources ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B sliverbar
.BI \-\-action\ MODULE\ OPERATION
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliverbar
is a C17 panel for Linux desktops running X11 and an EWMH-compatible window
manager.  It creates and draws its own dock window, reserves screen space,
handles mouse actions, and hosts XEmbed system-tray clients.
.PP
The panel provides workspaces, active-window title, clock, CPU, battery,
screencast, volume, network, brightness, weather, sleep inhibitor, application
launcher, system tray, and power modules.  Each optional module can hide itself
when its data source or helper program is unavailable.  An enhanced bspwm
workspace backend is available, with a portable EWMH backend as the fallback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\  PATH
Read configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the selected configuration without starting the panel.  Unknown or
invalid keys cause failure.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Print the selected configuration, display and workspace backend, optional
programs, fonts, application roles, launcher catalog, WLAN source, weather
locations, power actions, and inhibitor backend without starting the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-list-pim-sources
List Evolution Data Server calendar and task sources as tab-separated type,
enabled state, stable ID, and display name.  Credentials, DAV URLs, and server
addresses are not printed.  The command fails when EDS support is not compiled
in or the registry is unavailable.
.TP
.BI \-\-action\ MODULE\ OPERATION
Send a validated action to the running panel through its user-only runtime
socket.  Supported combinations are
.BR "volume up" ,
.BR "volume down" ,
.BR "volume toggle" ,
.BR "brightness up" ,
.BR "brightness down" ,
.BR "refresh volume" ,
and
.BR "refresh brightness" .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program name and version, then exit successfully.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration format consists of one
.I key=value
assignment per line.  Empty lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.  Start with the installed example rather than an empty file:
.PP
.EX
install -Dm644 /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf \
  "$HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf"
sliverbar --config "$HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf" --check-config
.EE
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-config
or
.BR SLIVERBAR_CONFIG ,
Sliverbar searches
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliverbar/panel.conf ,
.IR $HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf ,
the installed system configuration, and finally a local development
configuration.
.SS Display and workspace
.TP
.B font, icon_font
Pango font descriptions.  An empty
.B icon_font
uses the regular font and installed fallback fonts.
.TP
.B monitor
.B primary
selects the primary RandR monitor.  A monitor name or zero-based index selects
one output;
.B all
spans the X screen.
.TP
.B workspace_backend
One of
.BR auto ,
.BR bspwm ,
.BR ewmh ,
or
.BR none .
.B auto
prefers bspwm when a reachable
.B bspc
is available and otherwise uses EWMH.
.TP
.B height, underline, block_padding, title_max
Set panel height, underline thickness, horizontal module padding in pixels, and
the maximum active-title length. The native panel also ellipsizes the title to
the pixel width available between the left- and right-aligned blocks.
.TP
.B language
.BR auto ,
.BR de ,
or
.BR en .
.B auto
selects German for a German locale and English otherwise.
.SS Modules
Each main block has a
.BI module_ NAME
key whose value is
.BR auto ,
.BR enabled ,
or
.BR disabled .
Supported names are
.BR clock ,
.BR title ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR battery ,
.BR screencast ,
.BR volume ,
.BR network ,
.BR brightness ,
.BR weather ,
.BR timer ,
.BR inhibitor ,
.BR launcher ,
.BR tray ,
and
.BR power .
.B auto
hides a block when its required data or runtime helper is unavailable.
.SS Applications and menus
.TP
.B terminal
Terminal selection.  The default
.B auto
uses the system terminal preference and known portable fallbacks.
.TP
.B system_monitor, network_settings, volume_settings, calendar, tasks
Application roles.  Values may be
.BR auto ,
.BI desktop: ID.desktop ,
.BI command: PROGRAM\ ARGUMENTS ,
or
.BI terminal: PROGRAM\ ARGUMENTS .
Arguments are parsed but never evaluated as shell code.
.TP
.B application_launcher
.BR auto ,
.BR internal ,
.BR external ,
or
.BR disabled .
The internal launcher uses the registered desktop-application catalog.  An
external launcher is configured with
.BR launcher= .
.TP
.B power_menu_mode
.BR auto ,
.BR internal ,
.BR external ,
or
.BR disabled .
The internal menu obtains available actions from systemd-logind.  An external
menu is configured with
.BR power_menu= .
.TP
.B power_actions, power_confirm
Comma-separated ordered subsets of
.BR lock ,
.BR suspend ,
.BR hibernate ,
.BR suspend_then_hibernate ,
.BR hybrid_sleep ,
.BR reboot ,
and
.BR poweroff .
.SS Read-only agenda
.TP
.B agenda_provider
.B none
or
.BR eds .
The portable default
.B none
does not start EDS.  The EDS provider only reads sources already exposed by
Evolution Data Server; Sliverbar does not implement DAV or OAuth, read private
PIM database files, write PIM data, or create an on-disk agenda cache.
.TP
.B agenda_calendar_source, agenda_task_source
Repeat a stable source ID, use
.B *
for all enabled sources, or
.B none
to disable that type.  Wildcards and
.B none
cannot be combined with explicit IDs.  At most 16 explicit IDs are accepted.
.TP
.B agenda_days, agenda_max_items, agenda_max_undated_tasks
The defaults are 7 local calendar days, 10 total rows, and 2 undated tasks.
The accepted ranges are 1\-31, 4\-20, and 0\-5 respectively.
.TP
.B agenda_refresh_interval, agenda_popup_width
Consistency refresh in seconds (default 300, range 60\-3600) and popup width
in pixels (default 720, range 320\-720).
.TP
.B agenda_show_source
.B true
or
.BR false ;
defaults to true.
.TP
.B agenda_event_color, agenda_task_color, agenda_overdue_color, agenda_source_color
Exact
.B #RRGGBB
colors.  Dracula defaults are
.BR #8BE9FD ,
.BR #FFB86C ,
.BR #FF5555 ,
and
.BR #6272A4 .
.PP
Right click on the date/time block toggles the native agenda at the panel
edge.  Left click retains the calendar action.  Agenda rows open the matching
calendar or tasks role.  The popup stays disabled until at least one selected
source is reachable and does not take keyboard focus.
.SS Battery power profiles
When power-profiles-daemon is available on the system D-Bus and the native
popup is compiled in, left click on the battery block opens the profiles
reported by
.BR net.hadess.PowerProfiles .
The active profile is marked.  Sliverbar accepts only identifiers currently
offered by the service, sets ActiveProfile through D-Bus with interactive
authorization enabled, and reads the property back to confirm the change.
Without a compatible service the battery block remains visible without a
profile click action.  Sliverbar does not write power policy directly to
.B /sys
or invoke sudo, and it does not guess command backends for TLP or TuneD.
.PP
When at least one battery is present, right click toggles a native details
popup anchored to the battery block.  It shows only kernel-provided charge
level, status, current charge, full charge capacity, design capacity, calculated
battery health, and current values.  Missing attributes are omitted.  Systems
without a battery do not expose this right-click action.
.SS Weather
.TP
.B weather_location
May be repeated up to four times.  Its format is
.IR safe-id|Display\ name|service\ query .
.TP
.B weather_default
Selects the default weather location by its safe ID.
.TP
.B location
Legacy single-location weather query.
.TP
.B weather_interval
Refresh interval in seconds.  Values are limited to 1800 through 14400.
.TP
.B weather_image
Deprecated compatibility key.  Its value is ignored because forecasts are
rendered natively.
.PP
Left click selects among configured locations, middle click refreshes, and
right click toggles a native three-day forecast below the weather block.
For each day it shows minimum and maximum temperature plus four columns for
Morning, Noon, Evening, and Night, represented by the 06, 12, 18, and 21
forecast records.  Continuous vertical rules separate the columns without
horizontal row dividers.  Each column shows a weather glyph,
temperature, rain probability, wind direction, and wind speed.  Missing values
are shown as dashes, and monochrome Unicode symbols are used when no icon font
is available.
The popup header shows the location on the left and the last successful cache
update time on the right.  Older cache data also shows its date.
If a configured location cannot be fetched, the weather block stays visible
and shows placeholder values so the location picker and refresh action remain
reachable.
Only JSON weather data is downloaded; no forecast image or external image
viewer is used.
.SS Other commonly changed keys
.B volume_step
and
.B brightness_step
set scroll-wheel increments.
Internal displays use the kernel backlight interface through the active
systemd-logind session when available.  Other outputs fall back to software
brightness through
.BR xrandr (1).
.B network_interval
sets the network refresh period.
.PP
The network block remains visible without an active connection.  Ethernet and
Wi-Fi availability and signal strength use dedicated glyphs.  A ten-pixel
gap separates the Wi-Fi glyph from the rendered percentage.  Right click opens
an anchored menu with up to the three strongest visible SSIDs for which
NetworkManager has a saved profile.  A filled dot marks the active SSID, and
selecting an entry activates that profile.  Two spaces separate a menu signal
glyph from its SSID.  The menu is also available while Ethernet is active.
Opening it requests a non-blocking Wi-Fi scan and refreshes the saved-network
results once per second for up to five seconds.
Keys beginning with
.B color_
configure panel and module colors using values such as
.BR #191A21 .
See
.I /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf
for the complete, validated set of keys and portable defaults.
.SH EXAMPLES
A minimal panel containing only clock and title can use:
.PP
.EX
workspace_backend=none
module_clock=enabled
module_title=enabled
module_cpu=disabled
module_battery=disabled
module_screencast=disabled
module_volume=disabled
module_network=disabled
module_brightness=disabled
module_weather=disabled
module_timer=disabled
module_inhibitor=disabled
module_launcher=disabled
module_tray=disabled
module_power=disabled
.EE
.PP
Enable bspwm workspaces, the portable launcher selection, and tray detection:
.PP
.EX
workspace_backend=bspwm
monitor=primary
module_launcher=auto
module_tray=auto
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLIVERBAR_CONFIG
Configuration path used when
.B \-\-config
is absent.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, HOME
Used to locate the per-user configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used for weather caches, selected weather location, and the single-instance
lock.  Safe defaults below
.B HOME
or
.I /tmp
are used where supported.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Selects the X11 display.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliverbar/panel.conf
Preferred per-user configuration.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/sliverbar/panel.conf
Per-user fallback when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I /etc/sliverbar/panel.conf
Installed system configuration and example.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful version output, validation, diagnostics, or normal
termination.  Invalid arguments return 2.  Configuration and runtime failures
return a nonzero status.  Starting a second instance returns 200.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bspc (1),
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR pactl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR xrandr (1)
